{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":14690,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This family is expressed by almost all bacterial and eukaryotic genomes but not by archaea. Its function is to down-regulate protein synthesis under conditions of nutrient shortage, and it does this by binding to protein L14 of the large ribosomal subunit, thus acting as a ribosomal silencing factor (RsfS) by blocking the joining of the ribosomal subunits [[cite:PUB00064845]]. This family is structurally homologous to nucleotidyltransferases.","domain_architectures":103,"interpro_id":"","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":21269,"name":"Ribosomal silencing factor during starvation","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF02410","proteins":21229,"proteomes":20133,"short_name":"RsfS","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF02410","structures":56,"taxa":31990,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Added two scoped graphs with three primary-evidence edges, exact b0637 reference mapping, tagged-protein assay conditions and separate BW25113 whole-gene phenotype. Figures 3 and 4 were visually inspected. Retained the preassembled-ribosome qualification and native-promoter versus tac complementation distinction; later pre-50S and organelle contexts remain follow-up work.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054034Z-codex-d18469.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054034Z-codex-d18469.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054034Z-codex-d18469.yaml","summary":"Curate RsfS subunit-association, synthesis and media-shift effects","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:40:34Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/30a0601c713fdbf1080ab8c2cc0f5ea1ad264f59/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054034Z-codex-d18469.yaml"},{"action":"REVIEW","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Saved a partial scientific self-review for the exact current projection. Confirmed b0637/P0AAT6 mapping, two separate biochemical readouts and a distinct complementation-supported growth phenotype. Remaining organelle, reporter, competition and later biogenesis contexts are open; no REVIEWED promotion or publication.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054312Z-codex-62c707.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054312Z-codex-62c707.yaml","outcome":"needs_followup","source_path":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054312Z-codex-62c707.yaml","summary":"Review scoped RsfS biochemical and adaptation graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:43:12Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/30a0601c713fdbf1080ab8c2cc0f5ea1ad264f59/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054312Z-codex-62c707.yaml"},{"action":"EDIT","agent":"Antigravity","curator":"Antigravity","description":"Resolved Stage 4 review finding pf02410-media-shift-graph-missing-taxon (Issue #336) by adding taxon: NCBITaxon:83333 (Escherichia coli K-12) to the ecoli-rsfs-deletion-media-shift causal graph in curation/families/PF02410.yaml, matching the organism scope of PMID:22843840 and the sibling ecoli-rsfs-50s-binding-silencing graph.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-21T133500Z-antigravity-a13360.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-21T133500Z-antigravity-a13360.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-21T133500Z-antigravity-a13360.yaml","summary":"Add taxon NCBITaxon:83333 to ecoli-rsfs-deletion-media-shift causal graph","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:35:00Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/30a0601c713fdbf1080ab8c2cc0f5ea1ad264f59/history/records/PF02410/2026-10-21T133500Z-antigravity-a13360.yaml"}],"local_source":"source/data/families/PF02410.yaml","record":{"causal_graphs":[{"context":"Preincubate 18 pmol 50S with 180 ug poly(U) and with or without 360 pmol RsfS in 90 uL for 10 min at 37 C, then 10 pmol 30S for 10 min. Buffer contains 20 mM HEPES pH 7.6 at 0 C, 4.5 mM Mg acetate, 150 mM K acetate, 4 mM beta-mercaptoethanol, 2 mM spermidine and 0.05 mM spermine. Sister aliquots undergo sucrose gradients or precharged Phe-tRNA/factor-dependent synthesis for 2 min at 30 C.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"rsfs-decreases-70s-association","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02410/hauser-2012-rsfs.txt","cache_sha256":"227e2b3da32ac247a2cb804db6768c91b29af5b2e1fb8aad1ad31d91c38e6833","explanation":"Figure 4B, its caption and the poly(U)/gradient methods establish a purified-system perturbation and measured assembly endpoint; Figure 4 was visually inspected.","reference":"PMID:22829778","snippet":"significantly reduces the fraction of 70S ribosomes","source_url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article?id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1002815"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02410/P0AAT6-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"9e6b9e5426c92b4ac5edc074c2bf03e2c63711e16b60cb34ee0d73e4f1849239","explanation":"Current member/domain coordinates with paired UniProt locus and sequence-version facts; identity only, not independent causal evidence.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0AAT6/entry/pfam/PF02410/","snippet":"entry accession: PF02410","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0AAT6/entry/pfam/PF02410/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"Adding purified RsfS before subunit association reduces the 70S fraction in the A260 sucrose-gradient profile relative to the matched no-RsfS reaction.","object":"associated-70s","predicate":"decreases","subject":"rsfs-preincubation","support":"OBSERVED"},{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"rsfs-decreases-oligo-phe","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02410/hauser-2012-rsfs.txt","cache_sha256":"227e2b3da32ac247a2cb804db6768c91b29af5b2e1fb8aad1ad31d91c38e6833","explanation":"Figure 4A left and synthesis methods; this endpoint is directly measured rather than inferred from the gradient. EF-Tu, EF-Ts, EF-G, GTP and precharged Phe-tRNA are required assay components.","reference":"PMID:22829778","snippet":"down to about 20%","source_url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article?id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1002815"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"In the defined subunit-association reaction, RsfS reduces incorporation of radiolabeled phenylalanine into oligo(Phe) to approximately one fifth of the no-RsfS control.","object":"oligo-phe-output","predicate":"decreases","subject":"rsfs-preincubation","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"b0637 maps to UniProtKB:P0AAT6, sequence version 1, 105 residues; PF02410 spans 9-104. The experiment uses the tagged protein, not an isolated domain interval.","graph_id":"ecoli-rsfs-preassociation","limitations":"The two endpoints are measured separately in sister aliquots, not independent replication. Preassembled programmed 70S does not show the same strong suppression; no literally zero effect is claimed. Steric contacts from docking and binding assays are not separate observed causal steps. Human mitochondrial and later pre-50S biogenesis contexts remain separate.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P0AAT6"],"label":"RsfS addition before 30S-50S association","node_id":"rsfs-preincubation","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Associated 70S ribosome fraction","node_id":"associated-70s","node_type":"STATE"},{"label":"Poly(U)-dependent oligo(Phe) synthesis","node_id":"oligo-phe-output","node_type":"PROCESS"}],"scope":"Purified N-terminal His6-tagged E. coli b0637 RsfS, called RsfA in the paper, expressed in BL21(DE3); E. coli ribosomal subunits and purified translation factors.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:83333","title":"E. coli RsfS suppresses ribosome association and oligo(Phe) synthesis"},{"context":"Overnight LB cultures diluted to OD600 0.005 in M9, 37 C and 200 rpm; OD600 monitored up to 40 h. Complementation uses cassette-excised mutants and tac-driven C-terminal His-tagged RsfS induced with 0.2 mM IPTG about 3 h after transfer.","edges":[{"directness":"INDIRECT","edge_id":"deletion-increases-adaptation-delay","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02410/hauser-2012-rsfs.txt","cache_sha256":"227e2b3da32ac247a2cb804db6768c91b29af5b2e1fb8aad1ad31d91c38e6833","explanation":"Figure 3B-D and media-shift/cassette-removal methods; the deletion comparison and distinct unsuccessful native-promoter and successful tac complementation were inspected visually and in text.","reference":"PMID:22829778","snippet":"The forced RsfA expression could heal the mutant phenotype","source_url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article?id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1002815"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF02410/P0AAT6-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"9e6b9e5426c92b4ac5edc074c2bf03e2c63711e16b60cb34ee0d73e4f1849239","explanation":"Locus-to-family reference mapping, not proof of the cellular causal route.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0AAT6/entry/pfam/PF02410/","snippet":"orderedLocusNames: b0637, JW5090","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0AAT6/entry/pfam/PF02410/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The deletion strain shows an extended OD600 plateau after transfer to M9; induced RsfS complementation reduces the defect, supporting a gene-dependent, condition-specific phenotype.","object":"post-shift-delay","predicate":"increases","subject":"rsfs-deletion","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"The paper identifies the deleted locus as b0637, corresponding to P0AAT6 and PF02410 at reference residues 9-104. This is not a domain-specific perturbation or independent resequencing of BW25113.","graph_id":"ecoli-rsfs-deletion-media-shift","limitations":"The phenotype is a prolonged growth plateau after initial growth, not immediate death or a measured energy deficit. Native-promoter complementation failed under the tested conditions, while induced tac expression rescued; the two are not conflated. No direct metabolic chain from the in-vitro assembly effect is asserted.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P0AAT6"],"label":"Whole-gene rsfS deletion","node_id":"rsfs-deletion","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Prolonged post-shift growth plateau and adaptation delay","node_id":"post-shift-delay","node_type":"PHENOTYPE"}],"scope":"Whole-gene b0637 deletion in E. coli BW25113 derivatives versus matched wild type; separate cellular phenotype from the purified-subunit experiment.","scope_status":"PHENOTYPIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:83333","title":"RsfS deletion prolongs growth adaptation after an LB-to-M9 shift"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":14690,"domain_architectures":103,"matches":21269,"proteins":21229,"proteomes":20133,"structures":56,"taxa":31990},"curation_events":[{"action":"CREATE","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054034Z-codex-d18469.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"changed","summary":"Curate RsfS subunit-association, synthesis and media-shift effects","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:40:34Z"},{"action":"REVIEW","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF02410/2026-10-11T054312Z-codex-62c707.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"needs_followup","summary":"Review scoped RsfS biochemical and adaptation graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:43